---
For Travel UI work, read `/design/travel/CLEAN_REBUILD_PLAN.md` and `/design/travel/STRICT_VISUAL_SPEC.md` first. The approved reference is final visual authority. When repairing the existing Travel home, preserve valid business/data/navigation logic but replace/refactor conflicting presentation code and delete obsolete legacy UI. Do not hide the old screen, leave commented legacy views, maintain duplicate old/new Travel presentations, or stack negative-margin/transform hacks on old geometry. There must be one active Travel-home hierarchy and one source of truth for geometry. Use supplied signature assets exactly. Preserve a compact landscape card composition. Do not allow the itinerary button to force date wrapping. Dates cluster: small `DATES` label above, one-line range + title-case duration pill (`7 Days`, not `7 DAYS`), vertical rule, then View Itinerary. Do not render the trip count as a solid navy `3 Trips` pill. Remove the unexplained floating up-arrow. Reject watermarked destination imagery. Implement iOS and Android with the same visual contract and platform-correct insets/tap targets. Do not stop after code compiles: capture screenshots, compare against the reference, iterate, then run the cleanup audit and remove obsolete Travel-home code/assets/styles.
